<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vitebsk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vitebsk is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Western Dvina</a>. Recorded from the early 11th century as a town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> lands, it became the seat of its own princes in the 12th century and passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algirdas">Algirdas</a> married the heiress of its last prince around 1320. Later a Polish-Lithuanian and then Russian provincial centre, it is known as the birthplace of the painter Marc Chagall.</p></div>
